kerbridge (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=@URGENCY@

  Write here what the operator must do by hand for this release: a default
  that changed, a path that moved, a value only they can set. Then rename
  this file to kerbridge-config.NEWS.in, by removing __disabled.
  `debian/make-changelog` stamps the version in, `dh` installs the result,
  and the package manager shows it during the upgrade.

  Leave the file disabled when a release needs no work from the operator.
  The stamp takes the version of the build, so a note that is left here is
  shown again at the next release, for a change that is already behind them.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  @DATE@
